b250":"https://zenodo.org/record/23402379/thumb250","thumbs":{"10":"https://zenodo.org/record/23402379/thumb10","100":"https://zenodo.org/record/23402379/thumb100","1200":"https://zenodo.org/record/23402379/thumb1200","250":"https://zenodo.org/record/23402379/thumb250","50":"https://zenodo.org/record/23402379/thumb50","750":"https://zenodo.org/record/23402379/thumb750"}},"metadata":{"access_right":"open","creators":[{"affiliation":"Independent","name":"Ke, Hao","orcid":"0009-0001-2818-4986"}],"description":"<p>We prove that the classical two-colour Langton ant exits every square of side n within (13/4) 3^n + 4 updates, uniformly over all initial colourings and internal poses. For a rectangle with N columns and fixed height H, we obtain an upper bound of order N^(floor(H/2)+1). Rational potentials on the critical curve (a-1)(b-1)=4 have positive monomial increments: four-step costs give the square estimate, while pairing along the short direction gives the rectangular bound.</p><p>A related strict rational clock yields decidable complete-state reachability, two-sided orbit equivalence and a computable orbit normal form. The analytic proofs are accompanied by independent exact Laurent-polynomial checks, exact rational tests, finite-state audits, and Lean 4.30.0 proofs of the supercritical local clock and telescoping lemmas. The eight-page manuscript and self-contained source archive include the critical-potential implementation, retained evidence, reproduction commands and SHA256 manifests.</p><p>Version 0.3.0 strengthens version 0.2.0 by removing the factor n from the earlier square bound and adding fixed-height rectangular estimates. It belongs to the same preprint version chain.</p>","imprint_publisher":"Zenodo","keywords":["Langton's ant","escape time","rational clock","critical potential","rectangular domains","discrete dynamical systems"],"language":"eng","license":"cc-by-4.0","prereserve_doi":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.23402379","recid":23402379},"publication_date"